KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ vector deduced from an iterator pair: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  `std::vector v(a.begin(), a.end())' uses vector's
deduction guide from an iterator pair ([vector.overview]: vector(InputIter,
InputIter, Allocator = Allocator()) -> vector<iter-value-type<InputIter>,
Allocator>).  CBMC accepts the program but v.size() is not 3.
